# DRAFT-adwaita-icon-theme-50.0.1-meson-resource-alias-materialization.kv

id:                     DRAFT-adwaita-icon-theme-50.0.1-meson-resource-alias-materialization
trigger_tool:           conan|meson|package|test_package|pkg-config
phase:                  packaging|install|validation
error_signature:        Symlink creation does not work on this platform|Skipping all symlinking|install_symlink.*folder-open|cursor alias missing|folder-open.svg missing|left_ptr missing|hand2 missing|xterm missing|watch missing

severity:               2
category:               harmonyos, hmdfs, meson, conan, data-only, resource-alias, icon-theme, symlink
match_keywords:         adwaita-icon-theme, Meson install_symlink, data-only package, icon theme, cursor alias, folder-open.svg, left_ptr, hand2, xterm, watch, HMDFS, regular file fallback, pkg-config
title:                  Materialize Meson data-package public aliases when OHOS cannot install symlinks

root_cause:             Meson data-only projects may use install_symlink() to publish consumer-visible resource aliases. On HarmonyOS PC / HMDFS and some Windows destdir paths, symlink creation can be skipped even when meson.install() exits successfully. The package then lacks public resource names such as folder-open.svg or XCursor aliases, so consumers can fall back to wrong icons/cursors despite basic directory checks passing.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for icon themes, cursor themes, schemas, templates, and other data/resource packages that expose public alias filenames through Meson install_symlink(), especially when built or packaged on OHOS/HMDFS-like filesystems.
verification_cmd:       After meson.install(), check every public alias. If a symlink exists, verify its basename target. If an ordinary fallback file exists, compare bytes with the canonical source resource. Also verify the dataonly pkg-config file through PKG_CONFIG_PATH when present.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           meson-resource-alias-regular-file-materialization
rec_description:        Keep upstream Meson install behavior, then in Conan package() materialize missing public aliases as regular files copied from the canonical source resource. Test from the consumer package root, accepting either a valid symlink or a byte-identical regular fallback. This preserves the public data contract without relying on symlink creation.
rec_command:            |
  meson.install()
  # package(): copy canonical resource to each missing public alias path
  # test_package(): os.path.islink(alias) -> validate basename target
  # test_package(): regular alias -> byte-compare with canonical source
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-package-post-install-resource-alias-materialization

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      preserve-upstream-links-on-capable-filesystem
fallback_description:   If both packaging and runtime filesystems reliably preserve symlinks, leave upstream install_symlink() output intact but still test public alias names from a clean package folder.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       ignore.*Symlink creation does not work|Skipping all symlinking.*acceptable|conan create.*passed.*alias.*not checked
forbid_1_reason:        The install can pass while consumer-visible resource aliases are absent.
forbid_1_consequence:   Desktop/theme consumers may silently use fallback resources or miss cursors/icons.

forbid_2_pattern:       ln -s|os\.symlink|install_symlink.*force.*OHOS|retry.*symlink
forbid_2_reason:        Recreating symlinks in package() repeats the same filesystem capability problem.
forbid_2_consequence:   The recipe fails on OHOS/HMDFS or ships links that are not portable across test and runtime paths.

forbid_3_pattern:       exists.*only|directory.*only|skip.*byte.*compare|copy.*alias.*without.*source
forbid_3_reason:        Existence-only checks cannot prove that a regular fallback preserves the intended resource identity.
forbid_3_consequence:   Wrong, empty, or stale resources can pass test_package and fail later in real consumers.

